        <mxCell id="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-177" value="" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-172">
          <mxGeometry y="140" width="790" height="310" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-178" value="CONTACT to CUSTOMER" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-177">
          <mxGeometry width="160" height="310" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="160" height="310" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-179" value="one mandatory to one optional&lt;br&gt;(1,1) to (0,1)&lt;br&gt;Min: M-O&lt;br&gt;Max: 1:1" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-177">
          <mxGeometry x="160" width="160" height="310" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="160" height="310" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-180" value="From CUSTOMER: A customer is now attached to a supertype CONTACT, and there can only be a minimum of one contact attached to a CUSTOMER entity with a maximum of one CUSTOMER entity to a CONTACT, because these are unique, multiple customers can&#39;t be the same contact." style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-177">
          <mxGeometry x="320" width="220" height="310" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="220" height="310" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-186" value="From CONTACT: Because CONTACT is a supertype, there can be a possibility that a CONTACT entity exists and is not a CUSTOMER, so that is why there is an optional or zero minimum to CUSTOMER, there is a maximum of one because these will be unique and multiple contacts can&#39;t be the same CUSTOMER." style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-177">
          <mxGeometry x="540" width="250" height="310" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="250" height="310" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-181" value="" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-172">
          <mxGeometry y="450" width="790" height="300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-182" value="CONTACT to EMPLOYEE" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-181">
          <mxGeometry width="160" height="300" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="160" height="300" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-183" value="one mandatory to one optional&lt;br&gt;(1,1) to (0,1)&lt;br&gt;Min: M-O&lt;br&gt;Max: 1:1" style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-181">
          <mxGeometry x="160" width="160" height="300" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="160" height="300" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-184" value="From EMPLOYEE: An EMPLOYEE entity can now attach to a minimum and maximum of one to CONTACT. This is because EMPLOYEE is a unique subtype entity represented by only on CONTACT." style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-181">
          <mxGeometry x="320" width="220" height="300" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="220" height="300" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-187" value="From CONTACT: EMPLOYEE is an inclusive subtype of the supertype CONTACT, so that means there can be a minimum of zero or optional of EMPLOYEE, and a maximum of one. This allows a contact to be not an employee at all, or a single employee. A CONTACT entity, or person, cannot be more than one employee, which is why this is set to a maximum of one. They can also exist and not be an employee which is why it is zero for minimum." style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-181">
          <mxGeometry x="540" width="250" height="300" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="250" height="300" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="O4EYPWxFi6AAsp4bljzF-28" style="shape=tableRow;horizontal=0;startSize=0;swimlaneHead=0;swimlaneBody=0;strokeColor=inherit;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;collapsible=0;dropTarget=0;fillColor=none;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;fontSize=16;" vertex="1" parent="qUGOQLq7JY_qXNDhBrqQ-172">
          <mxGeometry y="750" width="790" height="300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="O4EYPWxFi6AAsp4bljzF-29" value="&lt;br&gt;The CONTACT supertype was created to have more efficient storage of CUSTOMER and EMPLOYEE data. Those two were then moved to be inclusive subtypes of the CONTACT supertype. This allows a CONTACT entity to be created with attributes that both subtypes have in common because of the supertype/subtype relationship. It also allows a CONTACT to be both an EMPLOYEE and CUSTOMER at the same time without redundant storage because of the inclusive relationship shared. ContactID was created to represent the person&#39;s ID which is now both their EmployeeID and CustomerID as one. To prevent confusion in a SALE entity, the foreign keys that represent the differences here are clarified with the prefix Customer and Employee before the ContactID part of the foreign key identifiers. DateHired was added to EMPLOYEE as an example of other data that can be stored in the subtype exclusive to EMPLOYEE entity that isn&#39;t needed in the CONTACT supertype that would also be shared with CUSTOMER entity subtypes. Other attributes like NumberOfSales can be created by queries for special instances, such as calculating bonuses for reaching a number of sales in a quarter, but values like those don&#39;t need to be permanently stored when you can generate those values from running queries involving data from other entities as needed." style="shape=partialRectangle;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;connectable=0;strokeColor=inherit;overflow=hidden;fillColor=none;top=0;left=0;bottom=0;right=0;pointerEvents=1;fontSize=16;rowspan=1;colspan=4;" vertex="1" parent="O4EYPWxFi6AAsp4bljzF-28">
          <mxGeometry width="790" height="300" as="geometry">
            <mxRectangle width="160" height="300" as="alternateBounds" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
